        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manville%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough sits where the Millstone and Raritan Rivers meet, giving it a strategic location that attracted industry and railroads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.manvillenj.org/240/Borough-History",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Manville lies on the Washington‑Rochambeau Revolutionary Route, the path that led troops to victory at Yorktown.",
